# CogniBooks_V2 Permanent Guardrails

## 1. Function File Integrity
- NEVER run partial search-and-replace edits on `netlify/functions/*.mjs` if a file has duplicate declarations; delete and rewrite cleanly.
- Always verify with `npm run verify:functions` after any function file changes.

## 2. Pre-Push Verification (MANDATORY)
Before EVERY `git push`:
1. Run `npm run verify:functions` — must exit code 0
2. Run `npx netlify build` locally — must exit code 0
3. Only push after BOTH pass locally

## 3. Deploy Trigger Discipline
- NEVER run `netlify deploy --build` concurrently with `git push`
- Let GitHub's webhook trigger a single clean deploy
- One deploy trigger per change set

## 4. Duplicate Declaration Prevention
- Before committing any `.mjs` or `.js` in `netlify/functions/`, run `node --check <file>` to catch syntax/duplicate errors
- Use `esbuild --bundle --platform=node --format=esm` to catch bundling conflicts locally

## 5. Environment Variable Hygiene
- All required env vars documented in `.env.example`
- Never commit secrets; use Netlify Dashboard for production values
- Verify env var names match between code and dashboard

## 6. Build Cache Invalidation
- When `netlify.toml` or function configs change, clear Netlify build cache before retry
- Use `netlify build --offline` for local verification when possible